Using 239 consequtive data for the lottery PICK3 (up to 9/3/2025) we use different forecasting tools to predict the result of 9/3/2025:	1	6	3.
(I keep some stacking moments in code - just for viewer experience. When I do melting/long transforming for data - of course it is should not be done  - conceptually the solution is correct).

All that is in the books: 2 Jupiter and 1 Colab. 

In the Colab book  we use some popular predictors from Darts Library as: 

NBEATSModel MULTIVARIATE
RNN: Vanilla RNN, LSTM , GRU
N-HiTS
Temporal Convolutional Network Model (TCN)
Transformer Model
Temporal Fusion Transformers (TFT)
Time-series Dense Encoder (TiDE)
Time-Series Mixer (TSMixer)
XGBoost Models
Kalman Filter Forecaster
TBATS (univariate)
Prophet
StatsForecastModel


In Jupiter books we predict with:
CHRONOS and MOIRAI
TimesFM

